{"1-7":{"people":[{"id":"ahab-h0256g","name":"Ahab","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"elijah-h0452g","name":"Elijah","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[{"id":"gilead-h1568g","name":"Gilead","kind":"place","brief":"In Manasseh","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"tishbe-h8453b","name":"Tishbe","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"cherith-h3747","name":"Cherith","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":3}],"words":[{"base":"H5158","lemma":"נַ֫חַל","tr":"na·chal","gloss":"torrent: river","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":141},{"base":"H3747","lemma":"כְּרִית","tr":"ke·rit","gloss":"Cherith","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H6158","lemma":"עֹרֵב","tr":"o·rev","gloss":"raven","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"H3383","lemma":"יַרְדֵּן","tr":"yar·den","gloss":"Jordan","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":182},{"base":"H8354","lemma":"שָׁתָה","tr":"sha·tah","gloss":"to drink","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":217},{"base":"H1320","lemma":"בָּשָׂר","tr":"ba·sar","gloss":"flesh","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":270},{"base":"H3899","lemma":"לֶ֫חֶם","tr":"le·chem","gloss":"food","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":298},{"base":"H8664","lemma":"תִּשְׁבִּי","tr":"tish·bi","gloss":"Tishbite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H8453","lemma":"תּוֹשָׁב","tr":"to·shav","gloss":"sojourner","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H0518","lemma":"אִם","tr":"im","gloss":"if","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1067}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JAS","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"Elijah was a man just like us. He prayed earnestly that it would not rain, and it did not rain on the land for three and a half years.","from":1},{"book":"LUK","chapter":4,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"But I tell you truthfully that there were many widows in Israel in the time of Elijah, when the sky was shut for three and a half years and great famine swept over all the land.","from":1},{"book":"LUK","chapter":4,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"Yet Elijah was not sent to any of them, but to the widow of Zarephath in Sidon.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":78,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"Yet He commanded the clouds above and opened the doors of the heavens.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":78,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"He rained down manna for them to eat; He gave them grain from heaven.","from":6},{"book":"LUK","chapter":1,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"And he will go on before the Lord in the spirit and power of Elijah, to turn the hearts of the fathers to their children and the disobedient to the wisdom of the righteous—to make ready a people prepared for the Lord.”","from":1},{"book":"1KI","chapter":17,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"“Get up and go to Zarephath of Sidon, and stay there. Behold, I have commanded a widow there to provide for you.”","from":4},{"book":"1KI","chapter":22,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"But Micaiah said, “As surely as the LORD lives, I will speak whatever the LORD tells me.”","from":1}],"notes":[{"id":"rev-11-two-witnesses","title":"The two witnesses","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2}]},"8-16":{"people":[{"id":"elijah-h0452g","name":"Elijah","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":3,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[{"id":"zarephath-h6886","name":"Zarephath","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"sidon-h6721h","name":"Sidon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"words":[{"base":"H6835","lemma":"צַפַּ֫חַת","tr":"tsap·pa·chat","gloss":"jar","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":7},{"base":"H9030","lemma":"נִי","tr":"ni","gloss":"me","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":908},{"base":"H7058","lemma":"קֶ֫מַח","tr":"qe·mach","gloss":"flour","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":14},{"base":"H3537","lemma":"כַּד","tr":"kad","gloss":"jar","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":18},{"base":"H0452","lemma":"אֵלִיָּה","tr":"e·liy·yah","gloss":"Elijah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":71},{"base":"H6886","lemma":"צָֽרְפַת","tr":"tsa·re·phat","gloss":"Zarephath","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"H7197","lemma":"קָשַׁשׁ","tr":"qa·shash","gloss":"to gather","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H8081","lemma":"שֶׁ֫מֶן","tr":"she·men","gloss":"oil","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":193},{"base":"H8033","lemma":"שָׁם","tr":"sham","gloss":"there","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":834},{"base":"H2637","lemma":"חָסֵר","tr":"cha·ser","gloss":"to lack","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":23}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"MAT","chapter":15,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"Taking the seven loaves and the fish, He gave thanks and broke them. Then He gave them to the disciples, and the disciples gave them to the people.","from":14},{"book":"MAT","chapter":15,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"A total of four thousand men were fed, besides women and children.","from":14},{"book":"2KI","chapter":4,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Now a man from Baal-shalishah came to the man of God with a sack of twenty loaves of barley bread from the first ripe grain. “Give it to the people to eat,” said Elisha.","from":14},{"book":"2KI","chapter":4,"verse":44,"verseEnd":44,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"So he set it before them, and they ate and had some left over, according to the word of the LORD.","from":14},{"book":"MAT","chapter":14,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"“We have here only five loaves of bread and two fish,” they answered.","from":14},{"book":"MAT","chapter":14,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"They all ate and were satisfied, and the disciples picked up twelve basketfuls of broken pieces that were left over.","from":14},{"book":"LUK","chapter":4,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Yet Elijah was not sent to any of them, but to the widow of Zarephath in Sidon.","from":9},{"book":"2KI","chapter":3,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"and he said, “This is what the LORD says: ‘Dig this valley full of ditches.’","from":14}],"notes":[{"id":"luke-4-elijah-elisha","title":"Elijah and Elisha sent to outsiders","kind":"type"}],"groups":[]},"17-24":{"people":[{"id":"elijah-h0452g","name":"Elijah","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":4,"firstVerse":18}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0452","lemma":"אֵלִיָּה","tr":"e·liy·yah","gloss":"Elijah","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":71},{"base":"H3206","lemma":"יֶ֫לֶד","tr":"ye·led","gloss":"youth","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":89},{"base":"H5944","lemma":"עֲלִיָּה","tr":"a·liy·yah","gloss":"upper room","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":20},{"base":"H7130","lemma":"קֶ֫רֶב","tr":"qe·rev","gloss":"entrails: among","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":227},{"base":"H1172","lemma":"בַּעֲלָה","tr":"ba·a·lah","gloss":"mistress","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H7121","lemma":"קָרָא","tr":"qa·ra","gloss":"to call: call to","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":733},{"base":"H5315","lemma":"נֶ֫פֶשׁ","tr":"ne·phesh","gloss":"soul","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":754},{"base":"H0802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","tr":"ish·shah","gloss":"woman","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":781},{"base":"H4191","lemma":"מוּת","tr":"mut","gloss":"to die","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":840},{"base":"H9030","lemma":"נִי","tr":"ni","gloss":"me","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":908}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":32,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"See now that I am He; there is no God besides Me. I bring death and I give life; I wound and I heal, and there is no one who can deliver from My hand.","from":22},{"book":"REV","chapter":11,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"But after the three and a half days, the breath of life from God entered the two witnesses, and they stood on their feet, and great fear fell upon those who saw them.","from":22},{"book":"LUK","chapter":5,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"When Simon Peter saw this, he fell at Jesusʼ knees. “Go away from me, Lord,” he said, “for I am a sinful man.”","from":18},{"book":"JHN","chapter":16,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Now we understand that You know all things and that You have no need for anyone to question You. Because of this, we believe that You came from God.”","from":24},{"book":"ACT","chapter":20,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"But Paul went down, threw himself on the young man, and embraced him. “Do not be alarmed!” he said. “He is still alive!”","from":21},{"book":"ROM","chapter":14,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"For this reason Christ died and returned to life, that He might be the Lord of both the dead and the living.","from":22},{"book":"HEB","chapter":11,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Women received back their dead, raised to life again. Others were tortured and refused their release, so that they might gain a better resurrection.","from":22},{"book":"1SA","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The LORD brings death and gives life; He brings down to Sheol and raises up.","from":22}],"notes":[{"id":"luke-7-elijah-widow","title":"Prophets who raised the dead","kind":"type"}],"groups":[]}}